 sleeps. Defaults to "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"nil"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"name":"customError","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The error to throw when the timer fires. Defaults to","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"TimeoutError.timedOut(duration:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"type":"heading","text":"Return Value","level":2,"anchor":"return-value"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A sequence of the same elements that throws if the upstream goes quiet."}]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"level":2,"text":"Discussion","anchor":"discussion","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The timer starts when iteration begins and restarts with every element, so it bounds the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"wait for the first element and each gap after it, never the sequence as a whole. Elements"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"pass through unchanged. When the timer fires, the upstream is cancelled and the sequence"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"throws, without waiting for the upstream to respond to the cancellation."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The upstream is read ahead of the consumer, and elements it produces while the consumer is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"busy are buffered, so the timer measures the upstream’s gaps. A duration of zero or less"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"throws before the first element."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":2,"text":"Example","anchor":"Example","type":"heading"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["let clock = ContinuousClock()","for try await line in bytes.lines.timeout(.seconds(30), clock: clock) {","    handle(line)","}"],"type":"codeListing"},{"name":"Throws","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":""},{"code":"TimeoutError","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" (or "},{"code":"customError","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":") when "},{"code":"duration","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" passes between elements, and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"any error the upstream throws."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"style":"note","type":"aside"}]}],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/afluent\/asyncsequences\/retryoncastafterflatmapping\/timeout(_:clock:tolerance:customerror:)"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/Afluent\/documentation\/Afluent\/AsyncSequences\/RetryOnCastAfterFlatMapping\/timeout(_:clock:tolerance:customError:)","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"minor":3,"major":0},"references":{"doc://Afluent/documentation/Afluent":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Afluent\/documentation\/Afluent","abstract":[],"title":"Afluent","role":"collection","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/afluent","type":"topic"},"doc://Afluent/documentation/Afluent/AsyncSequences":{"kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/afluent\/asyncsequences","abstract":[{"text":"A namespace for grouping related AsyncSequence operations.","type":"text"}],"role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"enum"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"AsyncSequences"}],"title":"AsyncSequences","identifier":"doc:\/\/Afluent\/documentation\/Afluent\/AsyncSequences","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"AsyncSequences"}],"type":"topic"},"doc://Afluent/documentation/Afluent/AsyncSequences/RetryOnCastAfterFlatMapping":{"abstract":[],"role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"actor"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"RetryOnCastAfterFlatMapping"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"RetryOnCastAfterFlatMapping"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Afluent\/documentation\/Afluent\/AsyncSequences\/RetryOnCastAfterFlatMapping","url":"\/documentation\/afluent\/asyncsequences\/retryonca